\mt1 Malachi  
\c 3  
\p
\v 1 Behold, I will \w send\w* my \w messenger\w*, and he shall \w prepare\w* the \w way\w* \w before\w* me: and the \w Lord\w*, whom ye \w seek\w*, shall \w suddenly\w* \w come\w* to his \w temple\w*, even the \w messenger\w* of the \w covenant\w*, whom ye \w delight\w* in: behold, he shall \w come\w*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*.  
\v 2 But who may \w abide\w* the \w day\w* of his \w coming\w*? and who shall \w stand\w* when he \w appeareth\w*? for he \add is\add* like a \w refiner’s\w* \w fire\w*, and like \w fullers’\w* \w soap\w*:  
\v 3 And he shall \w sit\w* \add as\add* a \w refiner\w* and \w purifier\w* of \w silver\w*: and he shall \w purify\w* the \w sons\w* of \w Levi\w*, and \w purge\w* them as \w gold\w* and \w silver\w*, that they may \w offer\w* unto the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* an \w offering\w* in \w righteousness\w*.  
\v 4 Then shall the \w offering\w* of \w Judah\w* and \w Jerusalem\w* be \w pleasant\w* unto the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, as in the \w days\w* of \w old\w*, and as in \w former\w* \w years\w*.\f + \fr 3.4 \ft former: or, ancient\f*  
\v 5 And I will come \w near\w* to you to \w judgment\w*; and I will be a \w swift\w* \w witness\w* against the \w sorcerers\w*, and against the \w adulterers\w*, and against \w false\w* \w swearers\w*, and against those that \w oppress\w* the \w hireling\w* in \add his\add* \w wages\w*, the \w widow\w*, and the \w fatherless\w*, and that turn \w aside\w* the \w stranger\w* \add from his right\add*, and \w fear\w* not me, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*.\f + \fr 3.5 \ft oppress: or, defraud\f*  
\v 6 For I \add am\add* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, I \w change\w* not; therefore ye \w sons\w* of \w Jacob\w* are not \w consumed\w*.   
\p
\v 7 ¶ Even from the \w days\w* of your \w fathers\w* ye are gone \w away\w* from mine \w ordinances\w*, and have not \w kept\w* \add them\add*. \w Return\w* unto me, and I will \w return\w* unto you, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*. But ye \w said\w*, Wherein shall we \w return\w*?   
\p
\v 8 ¶ Will a \w man\w* \w rob\w* \w God\w*? Yet ye have \w robbed\w* me. But ye \w say\w*, Wherein have we \w robbed\w* thee? In \w tithes\w* and \w offerings\w*.  
\v 9 Ye \add are\add* \w cursed\w* with a \w curse\w*: for ye have \w robbed\w* me, \add even\add* this whole \w nation\w*.  
\v 10 \w Bring\w* ye all the \w tithes\w* into the \w storehouse\w*, that there may be \w meat\w* in mine \w house\w*, and \w prove\w* me now \w herewith\w*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*, if I will not \w open\w* you the \w windows\w* of \w heaven\w*, and pour you \w out\w* a \w blessing\w*, that \add there shall\add* not \add be room\add* \w enough\w* \add to receive it\add*.\f + \fr 3.10 \ft pour…: Heb. empty out\f*  
\v 11 And I will \w rebuke\w* the \w devourer\w* for your sakes, and he shall not \w destroy\w* the \w fruits\w* of your \w ground\w*; neither shall your \w vine\w* cast her \w fruit\w* before the time in the \w field\w*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*.\f + \fr 3.11 \ft destroy: Heb. corrupt\f*  
\v 12 And all \w nations\w* shall call you \w blessed\w*: for ye shall be a \w delightsome\w* \w land\w*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*.   
\p
\v 13 ¶ Your \w words\w* have been \w stout\w* against me, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*. Yet ye \w say\w*, What have we \w spoken\w* \add so much\add* against thee?  
\v 14 Ye have \w said\w*, It \add is\add* \w vain\w* to \w serve\w* \w God\w*: and what \w profit\w* \add is it\add* that we have \w kept\w* his \w ordinance\w*, and that we have \w walked\w* \w mournfully\w* \w before\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*?\f + \fr 3.14 \ft ordinance: Heb. observation\f*\f + \fr 3.14 \ft mournfully: Heb. in black\f*  
\v 15 And now we \w call\w* the \w proud\w* \w happy\w*; yea, they that \w work\w* \w wickedness\w* are set \w up\w*; yea, \add they that\add* \w tempt\w* \w God\w* are even \w delivered\w*.\f + \fr 3.15 \ft are set up: Heb. are built\f*   
\p
\v 16 ¶ Then they that \w feared\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* spake \w often\w* \w one\w* to \w another\w*: and the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w hearkened\w*, and \w heard\w* \add it\add*, and a \w book\w* of \w remembrance\w* was \w written\w* \w before\w* him for them that \w feared\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, and that \w thought\w* upon his \w name\w*.  
\v 17 And they shall be mine, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* of \w hosts\w*, in that \w day\w* when I make \w up\w* my \w jewels\w*; and I will \w spare\w* them, as a \w man\w* \w spareth\w* his own \w son\w* that \w serveth\w* him.\f + \fr 3.17 \ft jewels: or, special treasure\f*  
\v 18 Then shall ye \w return\w*, and \w discern\w* between the \w righteous\w* and the \w wicked\w*, between him that \w serveth\w* \w God\w* and him that \w serveth\w* him not.   
\c 4  
\p
\v 1 For, behold, the \w day\w* \w cometh\w*, that shall \w burn\w* \w as an oven\w*; \w and all the proud\w*, yea, and all that \w do\w* \w wickedly\w*, \w shall be stubble\w*: \w and the day\w* that \w cometh\w* \w shall burn them up\w*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w of hosts\w*, \w that it shall leave\w* \w them neither root\w* \w nor branch\w*.   
\p
\v 2 ¶ \w But unto you that fear\w* \w my name\w* \w shall the Sun\w* \w of righteousness\w* \w arise\w* \w with healing\w* \w in his wings\w*; \w and ye shall go forth\w*, \w and grow up\w* \w as calves\w* \w of the stall\w*.  
\v 3 \w And ye shall tread down\w* \w the wicked\w*; \w for they shall be ashes\w* \w under the soles\w* \w of your feet\w* \w in the day\w* \w that I shall do\w* \add this\add*, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w of hosts\w*.   
\p
\v 4 ¶ \w Remember\w* \w ye the law\w* \w of Moses\w* \w my servant\w*, \w which I commanded\w* \w unto him in Horeb\w* \w for all Israel\w*, \add with\add* \w the statutes\w* \w and judgments\w*.   
\p
\v 5 ¶ Behold, I will \w send\w* \w you Elijah\w* \w the prophet\w* \w before\w* \w the coming\w* \w of the great\w* \w and dreadful\w* \w day\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*:  
\v 6 \w And he shall turn\w* \w the heart\w* \w of the fathers\w* \w to the children\w*, \w and the heart\w* \w of the children\w* \w to their fathers\w*, \w lest I come\w* \w and smite\w* \w the earth\w* \w with a curse\w*.
